// Flying = a block-legality Cant clause [CR#702.9b]: can be blocked only by
// creatures with flying and/or reach. Composite per the keyword
// classification; the carried name survives expand_all so Has /
// LoseAbility name paths keep matching. A KeywordAbility-kind macro: cards
// invoke it INSIDE the wrapper — `Keyword(Flying)` — so keyword-ness is
// always explicit. The engine evaluates point-wise Cant(Block) rows pairwise
// at block submission (decide.rs DeclareBlockers -> legal::block_forbidden_by).
//
// Written directly, not through the `KeywordAbility(...)` wrapper
// (`plugins/builtin/macros/macro/KeywordAbility.ron`) any more: that
// meta-macro's own param signature is exactly `{name, template,
// abilities}` with no `frames` slot, so a keyword that needs a `frames:`
// entry has to spell its expansion out by hand — same reason
// `Protection`/`Cycling`/etc. already skip the wrapper. This expands to the
// byte-identical registered `MacroDef` the wrapper form produced (Task 6
// pilot; see `docs/superpowers/research/2026-07-30-macro-frames/
// pilot-constituency-findings.md`).
(
    name: "Flying",
    template: "flying",
    kinds: [KeywordAbility],
    // Two frames, differing only in casing — a real, verified matching gap
    // Task 8's own G3/G4 canon sweep found. `frames[0]` ("flying") is the
    // citation spelling `template:`/G2 project against and is what compiles
    // — the legacy renderer force-capitalizes a keyword line's first entry
    // at render time regardless of the template's own case
    // (`crates/deckmaste_cards/src/render/mod.rs`'s `rules()`), so lowercase
    // is the right citation form there. But `CatalogAtom.spelling` — a leaf
    // field `unify`'s exact-value comparison reads literally — preserves
    // whatever case the *matched text* was actually written in, and this
    // pilot frame's compiled tree is a solo, one-ability `KeywordAbilityList`
    // that can only ever match a line that *is* the whole keyword line by
    // itself — which real oracle text always prints capitalized (line-initial
    // capitalization is universal for a solo keyword line). So `"flying"`
    // (lowercase) can compile but can never actually match a real card;
    // `frames[1]` ("Flying") is the frame that does. Both are needed: G2 only
    // ever projects `frames[0]`, so it cannot become the fix on its own
    // without also touching the checked-in `template:` field, which the
    // legacy renderer does not need changed (see above).
    frames: ["flying", "Flying"],
    body: Composite(
        name: "Flying",
        abilities: [Static(Cant(Block(
            on: Ref(This),
            by: Not(Or([Has(Flying), Has(Reach)])),
        )))],
    ),
)
